# Everything in this repo ends up inside a Linux container, so everything in it
# keeps LF endings regardless of the machine it was checked out on.
#
# This is not a style preference. An s6 run script with CRLF endings fails as
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/with-contenv bash^M" - the carriage return becomes
# part of the interpreter's path. The container then starts, the service dies
# instantly, s6 restarts it, and the log fills with a line that names a file
# which plainly exists. Checking out on Windows is all it takes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The images are bytes and must not be touched at all.
*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
